WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.060
On a volcano in Hawaii, an
observatory samples the air,

2
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.270
month after month.

3
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:11.820
In 1960, carbon dioxide stood
at about 317 parts per million.

4
00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:15.460
By 2020, about 414.

5
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:18.250
Zoom in, and the line zigzags.

6
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.480
Every year it peaks in May and
falls to a low around October,

7
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.240
a swing of about 6 parts per million.

8
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.550
Two patterns in one line.

9
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.400
What drives the yearly swing,
and what drives the climb?

10
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.160
In this mission, you'll
read the real record,

11
00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.810
and see that the climb is speeding up.

12
00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:42.100
Then you'll see how gases like carbon dioxide
absorb infrared from the warm surface,

13
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.830
and warm the planet.

14
00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:47.360
Your mission: explain what
drives the yearly swing,

15
00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.400
and what drives the long climb.
